<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83543" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλᾰτει-άζω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλᾰτει-άσδω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>slap with the flat hand</i>
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλατείᾳ</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				224
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>pronounce broadly,</i>
			like the Dorians, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				15.88
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλατεάζειν</span> (sic)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">: ἀλαζονεύεσθαι, φενακίζειν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλατειάδδοντες: οἱ γυμναζόμενοι τοῖς
				ἐφήβοις,</span> Id.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>